1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,589
… In January,

2
00:00:03,589 --> 00:00:07,259
the government named who it was hunting in Minneapolis.

3
00:00:07,259 --> 00:00:10,590
The worst of the worst. Vicious murderers

4
00:00:10,590 --> 00:00:14,564
, rapists, child pedophiles.

5
00:00:14,564 --> 00:00:20,944
They published a list of names. Then they arrested three thousand seven hundred eighty nine people.

6
00:00:20,944 --> 00:00:27,809
Then ICE's own records came out, and sixty three percent had no criminal record… Ninety

7
00:00:27,809 --> 00:00:33,959
seven percent were street arrests, pulled off sidewalks, not out of jail.

8
00:00:33,959 --> 00:00:40,939
These are ICE's own numbers…  It was called Operation Metro

9
00:00:40,939 --> 00:00:44,854
Surge, sixty days across the metro.

10
00:00:44,854 --> 00:00:50,994
The city never voted for it, never authorized it, and was never allowed to review it.

11
00:00:50,994 --> 00:00:57,569
When a bill shows up wildly bigger than what you supposedly bought, you ask for the line items first.

12
00:00:57,569 --> 00:01:01,710
Minneapolis got a two hundred three million dollar bill…for one

13
00:01:01,710 --> 00:01:06,400
month, and the agency that ran it is sitting on the evidence.

14
00:01:06,400 --> 00:01:13,274
Minneapolis got the invoice. ICE kept the receipt…

15
00:01:13,274 --> 00:01:16,904
Here's the itemized bill the city could put together.

16
00:01:16,904 --> 00:01:20,754
Lost business revenue, eighty one million dollars.

17
00:01:20,754 --> 00:01:26,159
Lost wages from people too scared to leave home, forty seven million dollars.

18
00:01:26,159 --> 00:01:30,809
Emergency rent help, fifteen point seven million dollars.

19
00:01:30,809 --> 00:01:34,359
One month, two hundred three million dollars.

20
00:01:34,359 --> 00:01:39,597
By April, the state attorney general ran the whole metro, over two hundred forty million in

21
00:01:39,597 --> 00:01:45,814
lost wages, around six hundred ten million in lost business, fear travels further than the

22
00:01:45,814 --> 00:01:51,154
agents do, people stopped going to work, customers stopped crossing the street

23
00:01:51,154 --> 00:01:56,510
…  So what did the money buy?

24
00:01:56,510 --> 00:02:00,070
At least three thousand seven hundred eighty nine arrests.

25
00:02:00,070 --> 00:02:05,930
Two dead American citizens. Renee Goode shot through her windshield by an ICE agent after she

26
00:02:05,930 --> 00:02:12,634
dropped her child off at school, Alex Pretti, and one more who died in custody.

27
00:02:12,634 --> 00:02:16,777
Then the full records came out through a freedom of information lawsuit.

28
00:02:16,777 --> 00:02:19,779
Fewer than one in four had any conviction.

29
00:02:19,779 --> 00:02:23,029
About thirteen percent had charges pending.

30
00:02:23,029 --> 00:02:26,099
Sixty three percent had neither, and the

31
00:02:26,099 --> 00:02:30,114
convictions they did count run down to traffic tickets.

32
00:02:30,114 --> 00:02:33,024
At least two hundred seventy three had valid work permits

33
00:02:33,024 --> 00:02:40,484
…  Now you might have seen a number going around.

34
00:02:40,484 --> 00:02:44,477
Seventy one percent flagged for violent or sexual offenses.

35
00:02:44,477 --> 00:02:49,340
That number is real, but it covers a hundred twenty four names.

36
00:02:49,340 --> 00:02:52,930
A slice of the list DHS published, three hundred thirty five names

37
00:02:52,930 --> 00:02:57,412
, out of three thousand seven hundred eighty nine arrests.

38
00:02:57,412 --> 00:03:00,835
That list is nine percent of the operation.

39
00:03:00,835 --> 00:03:05,725
DHS showed you nine percent. It left out the other ninety one.

40
00:03:05,725 --> 00:03:10,962
The press release showed you nine percent. The data showed you everyone.

41
00:03:10,962 --> 00:03:17,960
Minneapolis got the invoice. ICE kept the receipt…

42
00:03:17,960 --> 00:03:20,970
A federal judge was watching all of this.

43
00:03:20,970 --> 00:03:26,722
Chief judge Patrick Schlitz. He was hearing the detention challenges.

44
00:03:26,722 --> 00:03:31,884
On January twenty eighth, he counted ninety six violations of his own orders.

45
00:03:31,884 --> 00:03:35,625
By late February, the count was around two hundred ten.

46
00:03:35,625 --> 00:03:38,675
His words, ICE is not a law unto

47
00:03:38,675 --> 00:03:43,119
itself… He threatened criminal contempt.

48
00:03:43,119 --> 00:03:50,580
The operation kept going anyway…  Go back to Renee Good.

49
00:03:50,580 --> 00:03:56,625
The FBI first agreed to investigate alongside Minnesota…then it reversed.

50
00:03:56,625 --> 00:04:03,485
It took the car, the forensic evidence, the witness interviews, and locked the state out.

51
00:04:03,485 --> 00:04:08,662
Minnesota's request went to the same agency whose agent fired the gun.

52
00:04:08,662 --> 00:04:14,052
There's an old rule, Tuohy, that lets a federal agency head decide what outsiders get.

53
00:04:14,052 --> 00:04:19,149
Minnesota asked. DHS said Tuohy doesn't even apply here.

54
00:04:19,149 --> 00:04:25,755
The agency decided its own rules didn't bind it…  This

55
00:04:25,755 --> 00:04:32,575
newsletter keeps landing on the same logic in different stories, a cost that arrives without a vote.

56
00:04:32,575 --> 00:04:38,440
After the last election, I left Seattle. I moved back to a suburb of Detroit.

57
00:04:38,440 --> 00:04:43,309
I'll be honest about why. I wanted to be somewhere harder to find.

58
00:04:43,309 --> 00:04:47,160
I thought retribution would land on the blue West Coast.

59
00:04:47,160 --> 00:04:52,864
It landed on Minnesota instead, something I never wanted to be right about.

60
00:04:52,864 --> 00:04:56,204
There are two ways to answer a bill you didn't vote for.

61
00:04:56,204 --> 00:05:00,554
You fight it, or you get smaller so it might not find you.

62
00:05:00,554 --> 00:05:07,890
Moving to Michigan was the second kind…  Here's what couldn't fit in six minutes.

63
00:05:07,890 --> 00:05:11,760
A county attorney has charged an ICE officer with assault.

64
00:05:11,760 --> 00:05:17,044
Whether it sticks depends on doctrine that shields federal agents from state charges.

65
00:05:17,044 --> 00:05:23,934
Two cases are how you break that shield, and there is one lever even a presidential pardon can't reach.

66
00:05:23,934 --> 00:05:27,825
Every figure you just heard is sourced. Court records, ICE's

67
00:05:27,825 --> 00:05:31,830
own data, the state's filings, all linked.

68
00:05:31,830 --> 00:05:38,679
Minneapolis got the invoice. ICE kept the receipt… The full accounting is on Substack

69
00:05:38,679 --> 00:05:43,653
… That's at the Civic node.

